<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37453" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praecōnĭālis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		praeconnius, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to be praised</i> or <i>commended</i>, <i>that which ought to be
			honored</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">viri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Var. 9, 25</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pietati vestrae praeconiale est diligere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 8, 1</span></i>
			.—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praecōnĭālĭter</span></b> ,
				<i>honorably</i>, <i><span class="en">Cassiod.
				in Psa. 17</span></i>.</div>
